XSS Ke 3 Main Types
1. Reflected XSS

Payload request me aata hai.

Response me reflect hota hai.

Example:

Request:

/search?q=test

Response:

You searched for test

Payload:

<script>alert(1)</script>

Request:

/search?q=<script>alert(1)</script>

Response:

You searched for <script>alert(1)</script>

Browser execute karega.

Important

Payload database me save nahi hota.

Har victim ko malicious URL visit karna padta hai.

2. Stored XSS

Payload database me save ho jata hai.

Comment:

<script>alert(1)</script>

Database:

Saved

Ab jo bhi page kholega:

<script>alert(1)</script>

run ho jayega.

Dangerous Because
Admin bhi trigger kar sakta hai
Har user trigger kar sakta hai
Persistent hota hai
3. DOM XSS

Server vulnerable nahi hota.

Browser-side JavaScript vulnerable hoti hai.

Example:

document.write(location.search);

URL:

?name=<script>alert(1)</script>

JavaScript khud execute karwa deti hai.

XSS Impact
